// `unwrap` is the claim that a Result is Ok. When it is not, the claim is a bug in
// the program, so it stops through the fatal path `panic` uses: the message goes to
// stderr and the process exits 70 rather than continuing with a value that is not
// there. A caller that expects a failure to be possible uses `?` or `is_err`.
int function main() {
    Result<int, string> missing = result.err("the value was missing");
    print(missing.unwrap());
    print("unreachable");
    return 0;
}
